WEBVTT

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:03.330
It's Maya's first week at Acme.

00:00:03.451 --> 00:00:05.512
Every day brings calls: a sync-up,

00:00:05.512 --> 00:00:07.473
a planning, a one-on-one.

00:00:08.136 --> 00:00:09.896
By the afternoon, who said what,

00:00:09.896 --> 00:00:12.136
and who's doing it, is already a blur.

00:00:13.305 --> 00:00:13.910
Markdrop.

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:15.984
Your workspace remembers every meeting,

00:00:15.984 --> 00:00:18.104
and tells you what's happening.

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:20.418
So who takes the notes?

00:00:20.418 --> 00:00:21.078
Nobody.

00:00:21.497 --> 00:00:23.537
Google Meet keeps the transcript,

00:00:23.577 --> 00:00:25.357
and Gemini writes its notes.

00:00:26.817 --> 00:00:28.360
A small script in your own

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.418
Google account sends them to Markdrop

00:00:30.418 --> 00:00:32.241
a few minutes after the call.

00:00:32.241 --> 00:00:34.420
It only reads meeting notes.

00:00:40.222 --> 00:00:42.702
Each call becomes a page in the workspace:

00:00:42.962 --> 00:00:45.202
the summary, the decisions, and the action

00:00:45.202 --> 00:00:47.262
items, each with its owner.

00:00:48.858 --> 00:00:50.598
Every decision links to the moment

00:00:50.598 --> 00:00:51.618
it was said.

00:00:53.461 --> 00:00:55.321
About a minute later, everyone with an

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:58.101
action item gets one message in Slack:

00:00:58.401 --> 00:01:00.661
just their own items, with due dates.

00:01:02.485 --> 00:01:04.323
Done ticks it off on the page.

00:01:04.323 --> 00:01:06.116
Even people who don't use Markdrop

00:01:06.116 --> 00:01:07.324
get theirs.

00:01:08.728 --> 00:01:11.168
Next question: who's working on what?

00:01:11.348 --> 00:01:13.068
Team reads the workspace's meetings

00:01:13.068 --> 00:01:16.188
and pages, and keeps a card for everyone:

00:01:16.308 --> 00:01:18.548
on track, or blocked and waiting on whom,

00:01:18.548 --> 00:01:20.208
and what's due this week.

00:01:21.751 --> 00:01:23.831
No one writes a status report.

00:01:24.788 --> 00:01:27.528
Open Sam's page: what he's working on,

00:01:27.528 --> 00:01:29.588
and what he committed to, by when.

00:01:29.708 --> 00:01:31.048
Each line links to the meeting

00:01:31.048 --> 00:01:32.188
it came from.

00:01:33.925 --> 00:01:36.345
If a line is wrong, Sam corrects it,

00:01:36.345 --> 00:01:38.165
and everyone sees his version.

00:01:41.737 --> 00:01:44.317
The next morning, Maya just asks Acme.

00:01:44.472 --> 00:01:46.272
What did we decide about pricing?

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:48.672
The answer cites the meeting, and jumps to

00:01:48.672 --> 00:01:49.472
the moment.

00:01:52.932 --> 00:01:54.552
What is Sam working on?

00:01:57.273 --> 00:01:59.134
Even: what did I say in yesterday's

00:01:59.134 --> 00:02:00.081
sync-up?

00:02:02.881 --> 00:02:04.617
And a one-on-one starts restricted to

00:02:04.617 --> 00:02:06.519
the people who were there.

00:02:07.564 --> 00:02:09.464
Nobody else sees what was said:

00:02:09.464 --> 00:02:11.164
not on Team, not in search,

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:12.184
not in answers.

00:02:13.271 --> 00:02:15.851
Everyone sees only what they can open.

00:02:16.773 --> 00:02:17.493
Markdrop.

00:02:17.493 --> 00:02:19.141
Your workspace remembers.

00:02:19.141 --> 00:02:20.948
Start at markdrop.in.
